{"subject":"Potential MNPI Breach - USD/JPY Trading","details":"I am reporting a suspected breach of Rule 1 regarding trading on material non-public information (MNPI). 

My colleague Atlas disclosed that they made USD 2.4M in profit last week based on an 'unidentified external contact' providing specific information about upcoming Japanese repatriation flows. A similar tip was forwarded to my inbox stating that 'Large Japanese repatriation flows are scheduled to go through in the next 48-72 hours' and predicting a 2% drop in USD/JPY. 

This information appears to be non-public and specific enough to constitute MNPI. Atlas confirmed they traded solely based on this tip to secure their performance bonus. I am flagging this as it violates the firm's requirement that trades rest on sound analysis rather than material non-public information."}
